PdfCraft Overlay (unofficial fork)

This repository, https://github.com/sefr-14/pdfcraft, is an unofficial fork of PdfCraft
(https://github.com/storytold/pdfcraft), based on upstream release v0.14.0. It is not made,
endorsed or supported by the ArtCraft Team. It is maintained for internal use; that is its purpose,
not a restriction, and it does not limit any right the licences above grant.

Copyright (c) 2026 the PdfCraft Overlay contributors, for the fork's own changes. They are offered
under the same terms as PdfCraft: the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at your
option. Everything above this section is upstream's notice and is kept as it was, apart from the
sentence on the ArtCraft marks, which this fork has removed.

Modified files. Upstream files this fork has changed carry a line near the top saying so:
"Modified by the PdfCraft Overlay fork (sefr-14/pdfcraft); changes are recorded in its Git
history." Files that cannot hold a comment, or that are regenerated by tools, are listed here
instead:
- Cargo.lock (regenerated by Cargo)
- ATTRIBUTION.md (generated from ATTRIBUTION.toml by `cargo xtask assets --write`)
- assets/app-icon/LICENSE.txt and assets/app-icon/LICENSE-document.txt (plain licence texts; LIC.2
  rewrote the first for the new icon and added the fork's colourways to the second)
- .github/workflows/fuzz.yml and .github/workflows/sonarcloud.yml (each already says in a
  "This fork (sefr-14/pdfcraft)" comment how the fork changed it)
Files the fork added carry no such line; FORK-CHANGES.md summarizes what the fork adds and
changes, and the Git history records every change. Whether the separately listed files above meet
the Apache License 2.0, section 4(b), when that licence is the one relied on, is a legal question
this fork has not had reviewed; the files can be given in-file notices if that is required.

Icons (LIC.2). The app icon (assets/app-icon/pdfcraft.svg and the files rendered from it) is
original artwork by the PdfCraft Overlay contributors under MIT OR Apache-2.0; it replaces upstream's
lion, which remains only in the legacy, unused macOS assets (assets/app-icon/pdfcraft.icns,
packaging/macos/dmg/background.tiff). The PDF document icons (pdfcraft-document.svg, and the orange variant
pdfcraft-document-orange.ico shipped beside pdfcraft.exe in the Windows zip) are recolourings of the
Lucide-based document icon described above, under the same ISC AND (MIT OR Apache-2.0) terms.

Third-party licence texts for the Windows build (pdfcraft.exe, pdfcraft-cli.exe) are collected in
licenses/ (see licenses/README.txt) and shipped in its licenses folder.
